@startuml 05_order_sequence
title UML Sequence Diagram - Create Order (As-Is)
autonumber

actor Customer
participant "CreateOrderController" as Controller
participant "CreateOrderUseCase" as UseCase
participant "InMemoryInventoryAvailabilityAdapter" as Inventory
participant "InMemoryOrderRepository" as Repository
participant "InMemoryEventBus" as EventBus
participant "StockReservationConsumer" as StockConsumer
participant "OrderNotificationConsumer" as NotificationConsumer

Customer -> Controller: POST /orders (JSON)
Controller -> Controller: Map request to CreateOrderCommand
Controller -> UseCase: execute(command)

UseCase -> UseCase: Validate command and create domain objects

loop For each order item
    UseCase -> Inventory: isAvailable(productId, quantity)
    Inventory --> UseCase: availability result
end

alt All items are available
    UseCase -> Repository: save(order)
    Repository --> UseCase: savedOrder

    UseCase -> EventBus: publish(OrderCreatedEvent)
    EventBus -> StockConsumer: dispatch OrderCreatedEvent
    EventBus -> NotificationConsumer: dispatch OrderCreatedEvent

    UseCase --> Controller: savedOrder
    Controller --> Customer: 201 Created (JSON response)
else An item is unavailable
    UseCase --> Controller: InsufficientInventoryException
    Controller --> Customer: Error response
end

note over Repository,EventBus
Repository and event bus are in-memory
objects inside the same application process.
No PostgreSQL or RabbitMQ connection is used.
end note
@enduml
